cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research or software, please cite it as below. The proofs are unrefereed."
title: "Cartier–Miller extensions: normalized 2-isogeny closure, depth-three CM recognition and the rounded-third obstruction"
version: "2026.10.09"
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: MIT
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jordan
    given-names: David
keywords:
  - elliptic curves
  - Cartier operator
  - Miller algorithm
  - 2-isogeny
  - complex multiplication
  - central binomial sums
  - Gauss factorials
abstract: >-
  Extension research on Cartier–Miller evaluation of genus-one coefficient sums. It gives
  explicitly normalized coefficient recovery along rational degree-two isogeny paths;
  direct recognition through depth two from two ordinary easy seeds; one consolidated
  depth-three family (discriminant -192) with a CM trace preparation; and a proof that the
  missing boundary at the rounded third point p = 2 mod 3 is equivalent to the Gauss
  factorial floor(p/3)! mod p. Prepared with substantial generative-AI assistance;
  proofs are unrefereed and novelty is not claimed.
